==Physical appearance==
Second-century BCE [[Ottelia]]n historian [[DUDE]] described the Byrakans as tall, generally muscular, tanned-skinned, clean shaven, and [[wikipedia:auburn hair|auburn-haired]], with long hair that is tied up:
<blockquote>
The Byrakans are tall of body, clean shaven, and bronze of skin, and their hair is auburn, long and tied up behind their heads with ornaments made of wood or metals. 
</blockquote>

